{
  "_comment": [
    "P1 (recipe parity, kahan vs master on the 2B tower) and P2 (the 4B's measured footprint) of campaign/next-train-first-box-2026-10-06.DRAFT.json, as a tools/campaign_driver.py config. Written 2026-10-08 before any run; nothing here has run.",
    "NOT LAUNCHABLE AS SHIPPED: every placeholder is null, and the driver refuses an unfilled one. Fill them on the box (approved_by only with the human's yes on cost and the GH200 cycle), re-read usd_per_hour from the price page at launch, then: python tools/campaign_driver.py --config <this> --plan (verifies the pins and reads the box's uptime), then without --plan.",
    "Box (from the DRAFT, unchanged): Lambda 1x GH200 at $2.29/h, box_usd 12.0, wall_clock_cap_s 18000, both counted from boot (/proc/uptime). GPU work stops 45 min (the pull grace window) before min(12.0/2.29 h, 5 h) since boot; the Mac's pull fits inside the ceiling. At the ceiling the driver or its guard stops the unit's process tree and writes <state_dir>/BOX_CEILING. The terminate command does NOT terminate: no agent holds a cloud credential; the human ends the instance.",
    "Arms: v5's data argv (build/post-queue/box_q_v6x.sh SPLIT, 'verbatim from v5_common.sh V5_SPLIT') and v5's ft recipe (the same file's RECIPE less --noul-weight 4, v6x's one lever; agrees with v5 ft row 8079c966's recipe as copied in build/v6x/fixtures/v5rows.jsonl) except --optimizer; plus --max-steps 600 (with --epoch, which it needs), --score-val with a per-arm --verdicts-out (the per-row val results the paired bootstrap needs), seed 0, one --checkpoint-dir per arm with --checkpoint-every 100 (nonzero: the final checkpoint, which carries letter_log, is written only then). --max-steps makes every row quick (rule 8); each unit also declares quick, and the driver fails a unit that writes a non-quick row.",
    "expect_rows 2 per arm: the epoch arm's ft row and --score-val's eval row (real_ft_run --score-val help: 'write one eval row per seed'). The footprint sweeps (gh200_footprint.py --out, one file per optimizer), the reader and P2's tools write no ledger row. Their outputs live under <run_dir>/p1 and <run_dir>/markers, which 'carry' puts in every snapshot; each unit's log travels too. Checkpoints do not travel (no unit declares a checkpoint spec): the reader runs here, on the box.",
    "P1's reading is the unit read-p1: tools/read_p1_parity.py over the three arms (the final checkpoint epoch-seed0-cuda.json, the arm's ft row id filled by the driver from {ft_row_id:<arm>}, its verdicts) and the two footprints, --out <run_dir>/markers/P1_VERDICT.json. Its exit 3 (refused) fails the unit and ends the campaign before P2; the JSON it wrote stays. P2 runs only if that file's word == 'admissible' AND <run_dir>/markers/HUMAN_4B_DOWNLOAD_YES exists (the human's yes on the 4B download); any other word, or no marker within wait_max_s or the box budget, ends the campaign with P2 not_run.",
    "Pins: the qd-prep binary v5 ran (sha256 from build/v5-h100/v5_common.filled.sh and box_q_v6x.sh PREP_SHA256), the general fetch record (general_record_sha256 in v5-era ledger rows), the pre-dedupe drop list (campaign/v5-preregistered.json). Not pinnable by the driver (directories, or no recorded file sha256): v5_data_dir, decisions_pool, exclusions, backbone, snapshot_4b; real_ft_run records shard_hash and exclusions_sha256 in every row, which the P1 reading compares against v5's (108082545a66..., c38dd2ca3e8f...)."
  ],
